Dear Roger and all,<br><br>I know that this version is supersed by several ones, but I have a question that probably deals also with all recent versions. It is written :<br><br>• (MD9600 only) Use battery RAM for settings, so that if power is removed from the radio the last change to settings / channel / vfo will be retained<br>• Handle if settings can’t be saved to Flash because of Write failure<br><br>Does it mean that settings ar now only retained thanks to the battery RAM ? And so settings are no more retained in a part of the flash memory ? The battery RAM is not very reliable, specially if the transceiver remains on a shelf for a long time. <br><br>On my side I have kept the last stable version (R20240908), because of my misunderstanding of this new feature.<br><br>Thanks to all the team for the continuous developments, and best wishes for 2025.<br><br>73 - Jean-Roger<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=1970">F6EGK</a> — Wed Dec 18, 2024 6:59 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
